+# Foundational capability v2: scoped Capital synthesis
+
+**Mission status: NOT_ACHIEVED.** N853–N856 remain source_derived_unreviewed. External correctness and priority are UNKNOWN; no physical capability or complete-resource advantage is established. The frozen campaign report preserves full detail; this file records Capital-facing boundaries.
+
+N853 records a Laplace-positivity/convolution criterion for a closed convex cone C strictly contained in E with nonempty interior; pointedness is not required. It includes an adaptive radial strictly log-concave kernel with all exponential moments and no prescribed exponential margin, plus a separate r log r tail-class counterexample. Only the producer proof/root reconstruction carries that deep tail-class separation. The scalar PDE construction has a global lower bound above 0.183p; product/Gaussian routes fail in the recorded scope. Diamond–Essén novelty remains open.
+
+N854 records scalar-only exact acquisition of a fixed response map under calibrated independent additive rank-one controls, fixed source/detector and stable repeated reference. The weak-anchor indistinguishability result is a scoped robustness failure, not an exponential query lower bound.
+
+N855 preserves the exact ideal radial Pauli compiler and its decisive limit: the output law is classical postprocessing of an existing covariant spin POVM and is Blackwell dominated for state inference. The gamma-only covariance comparison and nonoptimal exact-all-t variance lower bound are separate statements. Finite precision/calibration remain open. Its N712 bridge is a protocol comparison only and transfers no Gibbs/Fisher theorem.
+
+N856 separates a conditional, unqualified isotope sequence from published gated-graphene active-control precedents. The purge ratio assumes positive D-loss; zero-D-loss with H escape is its infinite-ratio limit. The published experiments apply to their own device settings and establish no hBN, battery or isotope transfer.
+
+All eight review and capability gates remain open. Provenance and generated access provide evidence routes only; they do not close scientific or physical obligations.
