+Result: no material–support system is yet qualified. Park the device proposal; retain the mechanism.
+I did not identify a real material–support combination that establishes the complete passive de-trapping operation. The most informative lead is defect-engineered hexagonal boron nitride, or hBN, but the available evidence does not justify developing a mechanically constrained device from it.
+This is not a universal physical impossibility result. The present obstruction is more specific: the required responses have not been acquired under one realizable boundary condition, and the strongest material evidence exposes competing mechanisms that could make de-trapping unnecessary or counterproductive.
+The investigation changes the continuation decision. Further optimization of hypothetical relaxation energies is not warranted. Reopening this route should require one material-specific calculation or experiment that passes the qualification test below.
+No new first-principles calculation, molecular-dynamics simulation, or physical experiment was performed here. I inspected published experiments, calculations, structures and methods, and calculated decision thresholds—not material-response coefficients.
+1. What the material search established
+The earlier calculation remains conditional:
+\[
+\Delta B_{s\leftarrow A}=\chi(R_s-R_A),
+\qquad
+R_U<R_A<R_H.
+\]
+It permits a shared constraint to accelerate useful escape while suppressing a harmful transition. It does not establish that a support can access the required deformation, or that the occupied state is the state limiting useful transport. Those restrictions were explicit in the previous checkpoint.    astra_kardashev_transport_check…
+The strongest alternative material classes did not remove these restrictions:
+Material or operation	What is established	Qualification result for Astra’s mechanism
+Graphene-embedded crown ethers	Computational studies show strong strain-dependent ionic transport and transitions between transport regimes.	Relevant prior art for mechanical tuning, not evidence of a realizable stiffness-only support that also suppresses damage. arXiv
+Crown ethers confined within UiO-66 membranes	An actual confinement system: DB18C6@UiO-66 reportedly achieves potassium permeation of \(1.2\ \mathrm{mol\,m^{-2}\,h^{-1}}\) and K/Mg selectivity of 57, with dehydration and interaction screening central to its interpretation.	A credible existing confinement operation. The inspected evidence does not isolate the proposed occupied/transition-state compliance ordering or its damage counterpart. PubMed
+Strained \(\beta\)-Li\(_3\)PS\(_4\)	First-principles molecular dynamics predicts that selected strains change lithium site populations and conductivity substantially.	Destabilizing transport bottlenecks through strain already has a concrete materials formulation. It is not the same as changing accessible boundary stiffness at matched strain. APS Journals
