+Worked for 37m 46s
+I’ll recover the exact identity and tests, then assess realistic hardware against matched-cost alternatives, including acquisition overhead and failure cases that could change the control action.
+
+Developed the approach
+
+Reviewed Astra derivation, gradient tests, noise results, and repository checkpoints
+
+
+
+
+Refined the hardware design
+
+Designed the benchmark
+
+Optimized calibration overhead
+
+The central gap is certifying reciprocity: passive circuit construction may guarantee it, whereas limited port tests on unknown media cannot. I’ll also test whether simpler directional measurements suffice.
+
+A practical caveat is that transistor “resistors” need not be small-signal reciprocal. Moreover, transposing a small accessible nonreciprocal module may beat repeated port completion.
+
+
+
+
