+# Principal investigator reconstruction and evidence boundaries
+
+Root, 15 October 2026. This is internal scientific review, not outside validation.
+
+I read all three pasted texts. They supply research candidates and failures;
+their missing zip files, proof packages and audits were not needed or sought.
+The current theorem is derived from its explicit distribution hypotheses.
+
+For the convolution criterion I reconstructed the finite-order seminorm,
+cutoff necessity for measure noise, adaptive-step slope and derivative bounds,
+relative cone-radius error, normalization and exponential integrability. I also
+checked the independent sum-of-square-root construction and its interval bounds.
+The general cone statement now excludes the trivial whole-space cone, whose
+interior-distance formula would otherwise be undefined. No finite-dimensional
+proof obligation remains identified; external review and formal proof were not
+performed. The Banach-cone norm/distribution scope is exactly as written and
+does not cover arbitrary weakly normalized POVMs by assumption-free extension.
+
+I reconstructed the full-complex bound for the infinite-product Laplace witness:
+the compact-uniform product supplies exp(A|Re z|-c sqrt|z|), which dominates
+the second product's exp(O(log²(2+|z|))) growth. Smooth Paley--Wiener then
+gives an actual compact signed smooth density. Deep valleys force noise
+cumulant growth; the standard Legendre bound excludes every fixed r log r
+upper-tail class. No finite floating-point evaluation of the valleys is claimed.
+
+I constructed the scalar P=1+g_x²g_y² example and explicit L=5 kernel. The
+consequence investigator independently checked all derivatives and global
+inequalities, and supplied the stronger cutoff proof of product impossibility
+without assuming integrability of second derivatives. Arbitrary correlated
+Gaussian failure and unchanged-marginal/fourth-moment identities were also
+checked. Symbolic/grid receipts provide bounded supplementary diagnostics.
+
+For the qubit compiler I derived the shell-wave u,v expressions, checked both
+radial ranges of gamma-kernel positivity, and derived the stochastic
+postprocessing implementation. This proves statistical domination by the
+existing covariant spin measurement. The elementary variance gap uses its
+operator first moments, trace second moments and characteristic-function zero
+at pi/2. Quadrature is finite-cutoff high precision, not interval certification.
+
+For scalar control acquisition I reconstructed Woodbury, the pair quadratic,
+weighted-transpose invariance, triple-alignment logic, query counts and the
+proper algebraic exceptional-set argument. I checked the directed-cycle
+formula, strict dissipation, polynomial conditioning and limiting response
+gap. Opposite collective-action ranking is explicitly demonstrated at m=32,
+not asserted for every small even m. No equally informed model-fit baseline
+was executed, so no speed/cost advantage follows.
+
